## 5.5 **NEW:** Refactoring Existing Modalities (Breaking Changes)

Sometimes you need to replace generic sections with more detailed body parts (e.g., replacing "Upper Extremity" with "Shoulder", "Elbow", "Wrist").

### When to Refactor:
- Generic categories are too broad for patient searches
- Medical terminology doesn't match patient language
- Need more granular CPT code coverage
- Search results are too cluttered with generic matches

### Refactoring Checklist:

☐ **Document old structure** (CPT codes, categories)  
☐ **Create detailed replacement sections**  
☐ **Verify NO CPT code duplication**  
☐ **Update matchKeywords to remove generic terms**  
☐ **Update BODY_PART_ALIASES if needed**  
☐ **Test that old search terms still work (via aliases)**  
☐ **Update documentation with migration notes**  
☐ **Increase search result limits if needed** (see Section 6.3)  

