## 6. Search Engine Integration

### When to Update universal-search-engine.ts

You only need to modify `universal-search-engine.ts` if:

1. Your modality introduces a new keyword users might search for
2. You want the keyword to be recognized as a "modality" intent

### Adding a New Modality Keyword

Locate the `detectIntent()` function and update the modality regex:

**Before:**
```typescript
function detectIntent(input: string): "cpt" | "modality" | "bodyPart" | "mixed" {
  const normalized = normalizeInput(input);
  
  // Exact CPT code (5 digits)
  if (/^\d{5}$/.test(normalized)) return "cpt";
  
  // Modality keywords
  if (/^(mri|ct|xray|x-ray|ultrasound|us)$/i.test(normalized)) return "modality";
  
  // Common body parts
  if (/^(brain|chest|abdomen|knee|shoulder|neck|leg|foot|spine|pelvis|head|heart|liver|kidney)$/i.test(normalized)) {
    return "bodyPart";
  }
  
  return "mixed";
}
```

**After:**
```typescript
function detectIntent(input: string): "cpt" | "modality" | "bodyPart" | "mixed" {
  const normalized = normalizeInput(input);
  
  // Exact CPT code (5 digits)
  if (/^\d{5}$/.test(normalized)) return "cpt";
  
  // Modality keywords
  if (/^(mri|ct|xray|x-ray|ultrasound|us|pet|mammogram|mammography|nuclear|dexa)$/i.test(normalized)) {
    return "modality";
  }
  
  // Common body parts
  if (/^(brain|chest|abdomen|knee|shoulder|neck|leg|foot|spine|pelvis|head|heart|liver|kidney)$/i.test(normalized)) {
    return "bodyPart";
  }
  
  return "mixed";
}
```

### ℹ️ Note on detectIntent()

The `detectIntent()` function is primarily for optimization and analytics, not core functionality. The search engine will still find your modality's procedures even if you don't add the keyword here. However, adding it provides:

- Better query classification
- Potential future optimization paths
- More accurate search analytics

