## 7. Semantic Alias Integration

### Why Aliases Matter

Semantic aliases allow patients to use natural language:

- "heart scan" → matches "cardiac", "myocardial"
- "bone density" → matches "DEXA", "osteoporosis screening"
- "breast" → matches "mammography", "mammo"

### Adding New Aliases

If your modality uses specialized anatomical terms, update `BODY_PART_ALIASES` in `universal-search-index.ts`:

```typescript
export const BODY_PART_ALIASES: Record<string, string[]> = {
  // Existing aliases
  brain: ["head", "skull"],
  chest: ["thorax", "lung"],
  abdomen: ["belly", "stomach"],
  pelvis: ["hip", "pelvic"],
  elbow: ["forearm", "upper extremity"],
  wrist: ["hand", "upper extremity"],
  knee: ["leg", "lower extremity"],
  ankle: ["foot", "lower extremity"],
  shoulder: ["upper extremity", "arm"],
  neck: ["cervical spine", "spine", "head and neck"],
  spine: ["cervical", "thoracic", "lumbar"],
  
  // New aliases for PET/Nuclear Medicine
  heart: ["cardiac", "myocardial", "coronary"],
  "whole body": ["full body", "total body", "systemic"],
  liver: ["hepatic"],
  kidney: ["renal"],
  bone: ["skeletal", "osseous"],
  
  // New aliases for Mammography
